From: CervantesHallo <227578309+CervantesHallo@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [Cider candidate] Bound CPU retries before first ready-event owner acquisition

Requires0120 revision2, not selected by a recipe. Zero-timeout polls retain
one attempt; other attempts use load-before-CAS bounded at512. No event
readiness loop, lease shortcut, recovery or cancellation policy change.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@
 #include "wine/msync_coord.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(sync);
+_Static_assert( MSYNC_READY_TRY_SPINS == MSYNC_COORD_TRY_SPINS, "ready retry bounds" );
 
 static LONGLONG update_timeout( ULONGLONG end )
 {
@@ -1157,9 +1158,9 @@
 }
 
 /* Caller has a pinned cached event and holds its short Wine control guard.
- * No slow descriptor/TLV initialization, mapping, wait, recovery or notification
+ * No slow descriptor/TLV initialization, mapping, kernel wait, recovery or notification
  * may occur. Anything outside this closed CPU path retries under the old mask. */
-NTSTATUS msync_try_wait_ready_event( int obj )
+NTSTATUS msync_try_wait_ready_event( int obj, unsigned int max_spins )
 {
     struct coord_fd_record *record;
     struct thread_data *data = get_thread_data();
@@ -1180,7 +1181,7 @@
         !(event = coord_slot( obj, 0 ))) return STATUS_PENDING;
     __atomic_store_n( &data->msync_in_transaction, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
